From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:07:10 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 68/69] misc: samsung: scsc_bt: build the Bluetooth driver on
 6.18 as a native BlueZ device

Build the SCSC Bluetooth service, its shared-memory H4 transport and the
native hci_dev (scsc_bluez.c) on 6.18 (ADR-0008):

- the H4 read/write core works on kernel buffers; /dev/scsc_h4_0 read and
  write bounce through it (kmalloc/copy_to_user, memdup_user). The 4.14
  shim called the char-device fops with kernel buffers and NULL files,
  which user-copy rejects on arm64; it now calls the kernel core directly
  (blocking mode explicit instead of file->f_flags).
- h4_recv_buf() now takes a struct hci_uart: embed one, as the mainline
  non-UART drivers do (bpa10x, btmtkuart); depends on BT_HCIUART_H4.
- hdev->dev_type is gone; send_frame no longer reads the skb after
  kfree_skb (4.14 use-after-free) and frees it only on success.
- no Bluetooth address file and no SoC-UID default (no exynos_soc_info):
  random address unless userspace sets the bluetooth_address parameter
  before the service starts; the SoC unique ID is no longer logged.
- proc_ops, class_create without owner, no <linux/wakelock.h>.
- Exynos PM QoS hooks (legacy pm_qos classes) become no-ops; scsc_bt_qos.c
  is not built. ANT is not built.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ic43624bf814a0c620f94fd8953d6835803205431
